    "created_at": "2025-08-04T17:53:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-19T06:15:56Z",
    "body": "I do like to solve your problem According to the current Fetch specification (https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#scheme-fetch), `data:` URL requests are required to return a response with a \"Content-Type\" header, but there's no mention of a required or optional \"Content-Length\" header. This differs from `blob:` URLs, where a \"Content-Length\" may be more appropriate or expected.\nThanks!",
    "author_association": "NONE",
